One-liners (non-blocking, result via cal:
One-liners (non-blocking, result via callback):
  UltraCanvasAlert::Info(msg);
  UltraCanvasAlert::Successful(msg);
  UltraCanvasAlert::Warning(msg);
  UltraCanvasAlert::Error(msg);
  UltraCanvasAlert::Confirm(msg, title, [](bool yes){ ... });
  UltraCanvasAlert::Plain(msg, title);   // no severity icon

Rich form:
  AlertOptions o; o.severity = AlertSeverity::Warning;
  o.message = ...; o.details = ...; o.buttons = DialogButtons::OKCancel;
  UltraCanvasAlert::Show(o);

The message supports Markdown (**bold**, *italic*, `code`, headers, lists). The dialog height auto-fits the text and shows a vertical scrollbar once the content grows past the screen.

Every alert is modal and always-on-top; the parent window's input is blocked until the user answers. Severity picks the icon + colour (Info/Question blue, Success green, Warning amber, Error red).

showIcon = false (or Plain()) drops the icon column entirely, so the content spans the full width - use it when the alert body carries its own graphic that has to sit in the middle.

For a message that must not interrupt: a toast - see the Notification Toast page (UltraCanvasNotificationToast).

